            <section id="who-is-eligible">
               <h2>Who is eligible for Mounjaro?</h2>
               <div class="tab-content-sec">
                  <p>Mounjaro (weekly injectable pen), is usually prescribed for patients who fit the following criteria:</p>
                  <p>· Has to be aged 18-75 years old.</p>
                  <p>· Is diagnosed with obesity or has a BMI that is 30 or above.</p>
                  <p>· BMI of 27 – 30 with at least one weight related condition like prediabetes, hypertension, high cholesterol or heart problems</p>
                  <p>Mounjaro is not recommended or prescribed if you are:</p>
                  <p>· Below 18 years.</p>
                  <p>· Pregnant or breastfeeding.</p>
                  <p>· Having any kidney or liver related conditions</p>
                  <p>· Suffering from Inflammation of the pancreas (Pancreatitis), diabetic retinopathy, macular oedema, or other eye problems.</p>
                  <p>· History of thyroid issues or medullary thyroid carcinoma (MTC), or if there is a family history of MTC.</p>
                  <p>· Diagnosed with Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia syndrome type 2 (MEN 2).</p>
                  <p>· Allergic to any of the ingredients used in Mounjaro.</p>

