         <div class="faq-list">
            <button class="accordion-p">How does Mounjaro work in the body?</button>
            <div class="panel-p">
               <p>Tirzepatide, the active ingredient in Mounjaro, belongs to a class of drugs called GLP-1 and GIP receptor agonists. These drugs mimic the naturally occurring hormone GLP-1 which is released in the gut after a meal to suppress hunger. It also slows down gastric emptying to make you feel fuller for longer. This results in reduced intake of food which can lead to weight loss.</p>
               <p>Mounjaro prevents the conversion of excess sugar into fat by regulating blood sugar levels in our body. It is usually prescribed when lifestyle modifications have not been effective in weight loss.</p>
            </div>
         </div>
         <div class="faq-list">
            <button class="accordion-p">Mounjaro dosage guide for weight loss</button>
            <div class="panel-p">
               <p>It is important to follow a Mounjaro dosage plan to make sure that the medication is taken regularly to achieve the maximum weight loss and lessen the chances of side effects</p>
               <p><strong>Mounjaro dosing schedule</strong></p>
               <p><strong><img src="https://www.pharmacyplanet.com/media/wysiwyg/WLImage/Mounjaro_Dosage_Schedule.png" data-original="https://www.pharmacyplanet.com/media/wysiwyg/WLImage/Mounjaro_Dosage_Schedule.png" style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; width: 814px; height: 682px;" alt="Mounjaro_Dosage_Schedule" width="814" height="682" class="mf-loaded" data-was-processed="true"></strong></p>
               <p>If you are a first-time user, start at the lowest dose of 2.5mg per week for 4 weeks. As long as you are tolerating the medicine, your dose will increase to 5mg per week for the next 4 weeks and then to 7.5mg per week for 4 weeks. The dose can increase again to 10mg per week for 4 weeks, then 12.5mg for 4 weeks, and finally to 15mg per week. You can remain on this dose until your target weight is reached. This is known as the maintenance dose.</p>
               <p>Sticking to the dosing regimen of once weekly until reaching your goal weight is imperative.</p>
               <p>The potential for serious side effects is heightened when Mounjaro is misused. It is important to consult your healthcare provider before adjusting your dosage outside the established dosing schedule and to discuss side effects that might be affecting you.</p>
            </div>
         </div>
         <div class="faq-list">
            <button class="accordion-p">Buying Mounjaro injection for first time</button>
            <div class="panel-p">
               <p>If you are ordering Mounjaro for first time, each pen will have 4 weekly doses (one dose per week) lasting for 28 days. It is important to keep it refrigerated at 2-8C between uses, however, if kept outside of refrigerate conditions, the pen will be stable for at least 4 weeks before its effectiveness begins to be affected.</p>
               <p>Each pack of Mounjaro consist of:</p>
               <p>· Four needles</p>
               <p>· One Mounjaro Pen (4 doses)</p>
               <p>· Patient information leaflet and Instruction leaflet</p>
            </div>
         </div>
         <div class="faq-list">
            <button class="accordion-p">How to use Mounjaro Pen : A Step by Step Guide</button>
            <div class="panel-p">
               <p>Mounjaro must be injected under the skin (Subcutaneously) in your stomach (abdomen), thigh or upper arm part of your body. Make sure the selected injection site area is clean before inserting the needle.</p>
               <p>· Remove the pen cap and clean the end (where needle will be inserted) with a swab.</p>
               <p>· Take one needle from the pack, peel off the paper cover, and firmly push and twist the needle cap until it is securely attached to the Mounjaro Pen. Now remove the plastic cap.</p>
               <p>· Twist the pen until the first line appears in the Window. Hold the pen upside down and twist until a small liquid drop appears at the tip of the needle.</p>
               <p>· Twist the plunger until the number one appears in the treatment window.</p>
               <p>· Once the injection site is chosen, insert the pen at a 90-degree angle and push down the plunger gently until the zero appears again in the treatment window. Hold the needle in place for 10 seconds to make sure the full dose is administered.</p>
               <p>· Remove the needle and close the Mounjaro pen with plastic cap. Safely dispose of the needle.</p>
               <p>· Keep the pen stored safely for your next dose.</p>
               <p>Important Instructions:</p>
               <p>· Always check the expiration date and ensure it is not frozen or damaged before opening the pen.</p>
               <p>· A new needle needs to be inserted each time.</p>
               <p class="read-more-link content-description"><a href="https://www.pharmacyplanet.com/how-do-you-take-mounjaro" style="color: #2C596D;
    font-weight: 600;">Read More</a></p>
            </div>
         </div>
         <div class="faq-list">
            <button class="accordion-p">Where to inject Mounjaro for weight loss?</button>
            <div class="panel-p">
               <p>The best place to inject Mounjaro are the fleshier areas of your body. This includes your stomach (at least 5 cm away from belly button), thigh or upper arm area. It is important to rotate the injection site as inserting the needle in same place every time can cause irritation.</p>
            </div>
         </div>
         <div class="faq-list">
            <button class="accordion-p">Why does my Mounjaro have leftover liquid after the fourth dose?</button>
            <div class="panel-p">
               <p>You may notice a small amount of medication remaining in the pen after the fourth injection. This is normal and is included to allow the pen to be primed before each use. The pen is still intended to provide four doses only, and any remaining liquid should not be used as an additional injection.</p>
            </div>
         </div>
         <div class="faq-list">
            <button class="accordion-p">Will the new Mounjaro pen still have a ‘golden dose’?</button>
            <div class="panel-p">
               <p>From April 2026, Eli Lilly is introducing a redesigned Mounjaro KwikPen that contains less excess medication. The update is intended to reduce the amount of liquid remaining in the pen after the fourth injection.</p>
               <p>With the new design, there should be little or no medication left in the pen once all four doses have been used. This means the so-called “golden dose” or “fifth dose” that some patients noticed with older pens is expected to disappear.</p>
               <p>The medication, dosing schedule, and how the injection works will remain the same. The change only affects the pen mechanism and amount of excess liquid included for priming.</p>
            </div>
