         <div class="faq-list">
            <button class="accordion-p">How to manage the side effects of Mounjaro?</button>
            <div class="panel-p">
               <p>Common side effects caused by Mounjaro should not be severe and starts disappearing over time.  Side effects like Nausea, diarrhoea and heart burn can be resolved by following the tips below:</p>
               <ul>
                  <li>In case of diarrhoea, acid reflux and heartburn, consume small portions of meals and avoid spicy or strongly flavoured foods. This should help with reducing the level of gastric discomfort and get you back to normal in no time.</li>
                  <li>For vomiting and nausea, make sure to stay hydrated. Becoming dehydrated can cause other symptoms that can be distressing. Having adequate amounts of water, even in small sips, can help settle the feeling of nausea.</li>
               </ul>
            </div>
